{"title":"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The circumference of a circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> inches. The side of a square inscribed in this circle, expressed in inches, is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/1/0d153cad9e5e7304ce470e7216c9d4be5ff8b1b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{25\\sqrt{2}}{\\pi}\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }\\frac{50\\sqrt{2}}{\\pi}\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }\\frac{100}{\\pi}\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }\\frac{100\\sqrt{2}}{\\pi}\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }50\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"530\" height=\"41\" />    \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, find the diameter of the circle.  Plug in the circumference for the formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/1/0f1d9432deb6813aea854f31633a4e89d03b1b83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = \\pi d$\" width=\"59\" height=\"12\" /> to solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/e/5ce01d3633e9564527e94d7492209688814e931d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[100 = \\pi d\\]\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/0/6a0bc39d7182fcc2f04a1181879f48bd492fc5ec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d = \\frac{100}{\\pi}\\]\" width=\"62\" height=\"37\" />\nSince all of an inscribed square's vertices touch the circle, and one of the angles of the circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7dfa8a2a90d521b2b03f5b82a1fb9f85dce88c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />, the square's diagonal is the diameter of the circle.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/7/24707203747249e65ba033f4b1c2e36e3a5e43ba.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw(circle((0,0),50)); draw((-50,0)--(0,50)--(50,0)--(0,-50)--cycle); draw((-50,0)--(50,0)); draw((-3,47)--(0,44)--(3,47)); label(&quot;$\\frac{100}{\\pi}$&quot;,(0,-10)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>From the Pythagorean theorem (or 45-45-90 triangles), the side length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/2/ef245b332ba2ab246c95d81a52733d4e492c15a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{50\\sqrt{2}}{\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"45\" height=\"41\" /> inches, which is answer choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a2194b81820e8380be586c1564c3f5d03d5c100d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" /> .\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME\" title=\"1960 AHSME\">1960 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1960 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1960\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\